  "limitations": [
    "Private-use icon glyphs (close, back, notes and similar) may not survive shell text transport. Prefer a stable id or a captured path for those controls; the node path still points at the icon button.",
    "Before click/long-click/set-text, inspect Home/Reports until childVerified is true. The bridge caches this for the exact task; claim/release or observing the Child tab clears it. Forms do not show the child label. A child_not_verified reply means re-verify, not retry blindly.",
    "Selection-wheel controls (bottle type, weight/head, temperature slider, duration/hour-minute scrollers) expose few or no option text nodes. Use visual evidence and re-inspect after each scroll; do not guess option values.",
    "The Reports Week view can exceed the bridge reply limit. A truncated/timeout reply is not evidence that the click failed.",
    "Paths are capture-specific. Ids and unique text labels are preferred; re-inspect before any path action.",
    "Global BACK is mapped for recovery, but explicit close/back controls are preferred. From a root page BACK can leave Huckleberry.",
    "This catalog does not verify Firebase payloads. Use the parity workflow and an authorized observer before saving, deleting or starting timers."
  ]
